@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log for writing raw text. Each positional object is converted to a string with normal string conversion and the results are joined with ``sep``, followed by ``end``. Use it when you want the text written exactly as given.
+
+Compared to print, out does not pretty print containers, does not word wrap or crop the output, does not interpret console markup, and does not replace emoji codes. It does apply highlighting (on by default, controlled by the ``highlight`` argument, where ``None`` defers to the Console's highlight setting) and an optional basic ``style``. Here's an example::
+
+    console.out("[bold]Not markup[/bold]", [1, 2, 3], sep=" | ")
+
+
